%% W3D4 — Async & Parallel Tool Calls — Sequence Diagram
%% Shows a 3-tool fan-out: Tool A and Tool B complete within deadline,
%% Tool C times out and triggers a fallback before LLM context assembly.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User
    participant Agent as Agent Orchestrator
    participant DepRes as Dependency Resolver
    participant Dispatcher as Async Dispatcher\n(gather + semaphore)
    participant ToolA as Tool A\nPricing API
    participant ToolB as Tool B\nInventory API
    participant ToolC as Tool C\nShipping API
    participant Agg as Result Aggregator
    participant LLM as LLM

    User->>Agent: Submit query
    Agent->>DepRes: Analyse tool call dependencies
    DepRes-->>Agent: Plan: [A, B, C] are independent — fan out Wave 1

    Note over Dispatcher: Semaphore(3) acquired for all three
    Agent->>Dispatcher: asyncio.gather(A, B, C, return_exceptions=True)

    Dispatcher->>ToolA: wait_for(call_pricing(), timeout=1.5s)
    Dispatcher->>ToolB: wait_for(call_inventory(), timeout=1.5s)
    Dispatcher->>ToolC: wait_for(call_shipping(), timeout=1.5s)

    Note over ToolA,ToolC: All three calls in-flight concurrently

    ToolA-->>Dispatcher: price=$149.99 (312ms)
    ToolB-->>Dispatcher: stock=42 units (287ms)

    Note over ToolC: Tool C exceeds 1.5s deadline
    Dispatcher->>ToolC: Cancel coroutine (TimeoutError)
    Dispatcher-->>Dispatcher: TimeoutResult(tool_name=shipping, timed_out=True)

    Note over Dispatcher: gather() returns — all three results collected
    Dispatcher-->>Agg: [ToolResult(A, success), ToolResult(B, success), TimeoutResult(C)]

    alt All results successful
        Agg-->>Agent: Full context assembled
    else One or more results timed out or errored
        Agg->>Agg: Build fallback for Tool C\n"shipping_eta: data unavailable"
        Agg-->>Agent: Partial context with fallback markers
    end

    Agent->>LLM: Prompt with assembled context\n(includes explicit unavailability note for shipping)
    LLM-->>Agent: Response acknowledging partial data
    Agent-->>User: Final response (total wall time ~1.5s vs ~2.1s sequential)
